  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.69,
      "end": 4.63,
      "text": " Something fairly important is happening in the US bond market."
    },
    {
      "start": 5.15,
      "end": 9.79,
      "text": " The yield on the 10-year US government bond has crossed 5%."
    },
    {
      "start": 9.79,
      "end": 15.13,
      "text": " In fact, on 29th of September, it touched roughly 5.3%."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.13,
      "end": 18.35,
      "text": " It is the highest level since 2007."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.39,
      "end": 25.67,
      "text": " Now, a US government bond yielding 5% may sound completely irrelevant to someone sitting in India,"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.93,
      "end": 28.43,
      "text": " investing in mutual funds, gold or real estate."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.43,
      "end": 30.09,
      "text": " But it isn't."
    },
    {
      "start": 30.79,
      "end": 36.63,
      "text": " Think of the US Treasury yield as something close to the gravity of the global financial markets."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.49,
      "end": 43.97,
      "text": " If the US government is willing to give an investor more than 5% for 10 years,"
    },
    {
      "start": 44.63,
      "end": 48.51,
      "text": " every other investment has to answer a single question."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.45,
      "end": 52.59,
      "text": " Why should I take additional risk to own you?"
    },
    {
      "start": 54.38,
      "end": 59.76,
      "text": " Before we get into why this is happening, we need to understand two basic concepts."
    },
    {
      "start": 60.6,
      "end": 66.18,
      "text": " The Federal Reserve's policy rate and the US Treasury yield are not the same thing."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.04,
      "end": 70.22,
      "text": " The Fed controls a very short-term interest rate."
    },
    {
      "start": 70.68,
      "end": 75.82,
      "text": " Right now, after its September hike, the target is 3.75% to 4%."
    },
    {
      "start": 76.38,
      "end": 80.14,
      "text": " But the 10-year Treasury yield is determined by the bond market."
    },
    {
      "start": 80.14,
      "end": 86.36,
      "text": " If I lend money to the US government for 10 years, what return do I demand?"
    },
    {
      "start": 87.34,
      "end": 92.6,
      "text": " That depends upon what I think inflation will be, what I think the future Fed rates will be,"
    },
    {
      "start": 93.06,
      "end": 97.5,
      "text": " how strong the economy will be and how much additional compensation I want"
    },
    {
      "start": 97.5,
      "end": 100.26,
      "text": " for locking my money away for 10 years."
    },
    {
      "start": 100.96,
      "end": 104.04,
      "text": " And remember one basic rule of bonds."
    },
    {
      "start": 105.0,
      "end": 109.02,
      "text": " When bond yields go up, existing bond prices go down."
    },
    {
      "start": 109.02,
      "end": 112.58,
      "text": " So when you hear that Treasury yields have shot up,"
    },
    {
      "start": 113.16,
      "end": 117.38,
      "text": " what actually happening is that investors have been selling bonds"
    },
    {
      "start": 117.38,
      "end": 121.34,
      "text": " or demanding a higher return before they are willing to buy them."
    },
    {
      "start": 121.9,
      "end": 123.98,
      "text": " And this has been a very large one."
    }
  ],
